A||||4||Cozmo||Remounting 2.8 heads, any last min. tips & tricks??||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||03-30-2001||10:28 AM||||Gonna finally reassemble the top end of the Targa this weekend! Here's what I've got sofar...<BR>Heads redone: leak test OK, valve job, surfaced, springs checked.<BR>FelPro top end gasket set.<BR>New GM TTY head bolts.<BR>Exhaust manifolds welded and ported.<BR>Intake manifolds cleaned and gasket matched.<BR>Everything cleaned up and ready to go...<BR>Questions:<BR>1) Am gonna use Saturn hardware and anti-seize compound for exhaust manifold attachment (P/N 21006951, studs, 12 ea. and P/N 11502609, flange bolts, 15 ea.). How do I torque this? The book says 18 ft/lbs. What gets torqued? The stud, nut or both?  Do I copper coat spray the FelPro gaskets or use them plain?<BR>2) Exhaust manifolds are bead blasted now, very clean and shiny. What paint will stand up on these puppies? Can I use 1200' Bar-B-Que black rust-oleum?<BR>3) Thinking of replacing all the plastic vacuum lines with metal tubing and new rubber connectors. The local model train store has a great selection of brass, copper and aluminium tubing. What metal would be best?<BR>4) New distributor O-ring. Should I change the pickup while I'm in there?<BR>5) Head bolts go through to the water jacket. Do I use teflon tape on them, antiseize compound, both, or anything else?<BR>6) Anything I can do to the TB? Match it to the intake manifold?<P>I realize these topics have been addressed many times before (This forum's archives have been super!), I'm just feeling a little apprehensive <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> now that I'm actually going to put it together... This is the biggest wrench job I've attempted so far. Even tho I'll have a couple of mechanic friends around to help drink my beer, I'd love to hear any suggestions from fellow Fieroites! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Thanks  <BR><P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 2M6 Targa<BR>'86 GT<BR>'87 Coupe||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-30-2001||10:54 AM||||I also 'O' ringed the heads on mine. If your headgasket set dont have stainless ring, id do it.Since its already out, Id put in new pickup coil and 'o' ring, cheap and cant hurt.they make a special sealer for headbolts/waterjacket. Ive never found any paint that stood up to the heat. Those suckers really get hot, even header paint burns off. Prob leave them or powder coat them.<P>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-30-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||operator64||03-30-2001||12:35 PM||||   Well to the paint idea i have used just regular old white spray paint on the exhaust on my 250r racing three wheeler and it works great as for the exhaust manifolds on the fiero i have yet to try it. Let me know if you try it and how it comes out.<BR>       OPERATOR64||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||03-30-2001||02:49 PM||||An old trick for ensuring the head gaskets seal really well: paint them with chrome paint before installing them, and install them while the paint is still wet. Makes 'em seal great!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||03-30-2001||06:10 PM||||You should use new head bolts, about $27 for the set at AutoZone.  I used teflon pipe sealant on the head bolt threads. I used Dupli-Color 1200F black on the manifolds.  So far, it's still on them, but I don't put many miles on my car.||||reg||1
